  "summary": "Why corporate group health insurance leaves employees with massive hospital deductions: room rent sub-limits, consumables exclusions, and co-pays. Hook: 'Relying only on your company health insurance? One hidden clause could leave you with 40% of the hospital bill.'",
  "notes": "- Analysis of corporate group mediclaim policies in India and why employees face shock out-of-pocket deductions\n- Room rent sub-limits (1-2% of sum insured): choosing a private room above the cap triggers proportional deductions across ALL doctor, surgeon, and diagnostic fees\n- Consumable non-payable expenses (PPE kits, gloves, syringes, surgical tools) routinely account for 10-25% of total hospital bills\n- Corporate dependency hazard: losing insurance protection immediately upon job transition or layoff\n- Actionable strategy: purchasing a standalone personal super top-up policy with high deductible to lock in lifetime insurability\n- Directly aligns with user decision on first job financial roadmap series",
